# Licences in this repository

Three different things live here under three different terms. This file says
which is which, because the project's promise — that anyone can take the data
and use it without asking — is only worth something if it is exactly true.

## 1. The data — ODbL 1.0

Everything under `products/` and `schemas/`: the facts, the fact definitions
and their explanations.

Licensed under the [Open Database License v1.0](https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/).
Use it, including commercially. Attribute Open Catalogue. If you publish a
derived database, publish it open too.

Facts are not copyrightable in India (*Eastern Book Company v. D.B. Modak*,
2008 (1) SCC 1). A waiting period, a fee, an ingredient list, a battery
capacity — nobody owns these. We assemble, check and date them, and we give
the result away.

## 2. The code — closed source, all rights reserved

Everything under `src/` and `tools/`: the validator, the formatter, the
importers, the fetch scripts and every other program in this repository.

Copyright (c) Open Catalogue. All rights reserved.

**This code is closed source. It is not open source, and being visible in a
public repository does not make it so.** Source-available and open-source are
different things: you may read this code, and that is all. No permission is
granted to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell or
create derivative works from it, in whole or in part.

If you want any of that, ask.

It is readable for one reason: a fact registry that will not show its working
is asking to be trusted rather than checked. You can see exactly how any
number here was fetched, parsed and validated, and tell us where we got it
wrong. That is the extent of the grant, and it is deliberate — the crawlers,
importers and validation rules are the part of this project that took work to
build and that we keep. The data they produce is the part we give away.

Note for the avoidance of doubt: an MIT, Apache or similar notice has never
applied to this code. Where an earlier version of this repository said "code:
MIT", that was an error, corrected here.

## 3. The source documents — not ours

Everything under `documents/`: policy wordings, MITCs, prospectuses, brochures,
scheme information documents and the like.

**These files are the property of the issuer or manufacturer that published
them** — the insurer, the bank, the asset management company, the brand. Each
is protected by their copyright. Open Catalogue claims no ownership of them,
grants no licence over them, and does not relicense them under ODbL or any
other terms.

They are mirrored here for one reason: so that a fact this registry publishes
can be checked against the document it was read from, by anyone, without
asking us and without trusting us.

Our undertaking to the publishers whose documents these are:

**We do not modify them.** Every file is stored byte-for-byte as it was served,
under the filename it was served with. Each directory carries a manifest
recording the source URL of every file, so anyone — including the publisher —
can re-download and verify that nothing was altered.

**We do not make money from them.** This project carries no advertising, no
sponsored placement and no paid ranking; nothing here is for sale, and no part
of it is monetised, directly or indirectly. That is the project's founding
premise, not a concession made for this file.

**We remove on request.** If you published one of these documents and would
rather it were not mirrored here, say so and it will be taken down. The
manifest of source URLs stays, so the facts remain checkable against your own
site.

We consider this fair dealing for the purpose of verifying published facts,
under §52 of the Copyright Act, 1957. These are documents their publishers
distribute freely and, in the case of regulated financial products, are
required by IRDAI or RBI to make public.

## In short

| Path | What it is | Terms |
|---|---|---|
| `products/`, `schemas/` | The facts and their definitions | ODbL 1.0 — take them |
| `src/`, `tools/` | The code that checks and imports them | Closed source — read it, don't reuse it |
| `documents/` | Source documents, mirrored unmodified | The publisher's. Not ours to license. |

If you want the facts, take them; that is what this exists for. If you want to
redistribute a source document, get it from the publisher — every source URL is
in the manifests.
